s/cm2), rather pale brown in colour. It looks as if the strips have been fixed in position using gum arabic or another adhesive. There is some damage to the bandages, especially on the ventral side of the mummy. A separate strip of unknown function is stuck against part of the left side of the mummy. At the head end there are no concentric bandages but merely the underlying cloth. This has a dark brown to black colour and is much coarser (c. 9 x 18 threads/cm2). The cloth has been modelled to form two ridges over the original eyes and is fastened by some irregular straps of fine yarn. There are no traces of resin or bitumen."]},"dcIdentifier":{"def":["AMM 16k"]},"dcRights":{"def":["Creative Commons By-licensie: bron: Rijksmuseum van Oudheden, Leiden"]},"dcSubject":{"def":["krokodil"]},"dcTitle":{"def":["mummie ; reptiel ; krokodil ; dierenmummie"]},"dcType":{"def":["mummie ; reptiel ; krokodil ; dierenmummie"]},"dctermsExtent":{"def":["28,5 x 4,8 x 3,6 cm"]},"dctermsIsReferencedBy":{"def":["Leemans, Description raisonnée (1840) N 32 Boeser, Catalogus (1907) E.XLV.27 M.J. Raven/W.K. Taconis, Egyptian mummies (Turnhout 2005), cat. 117 cat. Fascinating mummies, highlights of the exhibition (Edinburgh 2012), 34 C. Greco, Mòmies Egípcies, El Secret de la Vida Eterna (2012) 202, 202 cat. 224"]},"dctermsMedium":{"def":["organisch ; mummie (dierlijk) ; linnen"]},"proxyIn":["/aggregation/provider/2021606/resource_document_rijksmuseum_van_oudheden_AMM16k"],"proxyFor":"/item/2021606/resource_document_rijksmuseum_van_oudheden_AMM16k","edmType":"IMAGE","europeanaProxy":false}],"timestamp_created":"2024-03-06T11:01:28.214Z","timestamp_created_epoch":1709722888214,"timestamp_update":"2024-03-06T11:01:28.214Z","timestamp_update_epoch":1709722888214,"type":"IMAGE"}}